    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] It was the family home of the late Cherry Drummond, 16th Baroness Strange.\n[2] Adam Drummond (31 January 1713 – 17 June 1786), 11th of Lennoch and 4th of Megginch in Perthshire, was a Scottish merchant, banker and Member of Parliament.\n[3] Sir John Gladstone of Fasque, 1st Baronet, FRSE LLD (11 December 1764 – 7 December 1851) was a Scottish merchant, slave-trader, Member of Parliament, and the father of the British Prime Minister William Ewart Gladstone.\n[4] It is now occupied by Lady Strange's daughter Catherine Star Violetta Herdman and her husband."
